{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Godly Qualities: a past life story","html":"<article id='ja6'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Jātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Stories of Past Lives 6 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Apaṇṇakavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Sure Bet </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>6. Devadhammajātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Godly Qualities: a past life story </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Hiriottappasampannā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Endowed with conscience and prudence, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>sukkadhammasamāhitā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and comprised of bright qualities, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Santo sappurisā loke, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>the good and true persons in the world </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>devadhammāti vuccare”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>are said to have godly qualities. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>Devadhammajātakaṁ chaṭṭhaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
